      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T14:45:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The exponents only have (1 \u003c\u003c 6), since they don\u0027t have the same range. Instead we should map `SK_GAMMA_CONTRAST` and `SK_GAMMA_EXPONENT` the way any requested values would be. In fact, it\u0027s a bit silly that this method takes floats, at least for the key.\n\nThat being said, it isn\u0027t super simple to compile time run `SK_GAMMA_CONTRAST` and `SK_GAMMA_EXPONENT` through the current code because of the use of `floor` which isn\u0027t `constexpr`.\n\nInstead of adding another special case cache here, it\u0027s probably better to have a generic cache (with maybe 2 or 3 entries). Before we do that we should probably get rid of the distinction between `paintGamma` and `deviceGamma`. It\u0027s far more correct to treat the differently, but we cannot generally let them be different because currently force coverage to be [0, 1] and allowing them to be different would require coverage values outside this range. I\u0027ll take a look into removing the `paintGamma`.",
